  "id": "COMPOUND:6779 - PROTEIN:3375",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between the compound (2Z,3E)-2,3'-biindole-2',3(1H,1'H)-dione 3-{O-[(3R)-3,4-dihydroxybutyl]oxime} and Ras-related protein Rap-2a, mediated through a common intermediate, 6-Hydroxy-5-undecyl-4,7-benzothiazoledione. This compound is identified as a target of multiple pathways, with the same intermediate acting as a bridge to Rap-2a across different target subunits, including Cytochrome b-c1 complex subunits 6 and 2, as well as Rieske. The shared mechanism of action implies that the compound may interact with mitochondrial components, potentially influencing Ras-related signaling pathways. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, highlighting a possible role in modulating Ras activity through mitochondrial pathways, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
